From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Lund <mrlund@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:54:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 50/66] Revert "wifi: ath12k: no rfkill GPIO on peach"

This reverts commit 2499c421ac05fc8b5d802d6fc14cbfd085e9bce8.

Obsolete on 7.3: the WCN7860 entry (cloned from QCC2072) has
rfkill_pin = 0, and ath12k_mac_rfkill_config() returns -EOPNOTSUPP
for that, which ath12k_core_qmi_firmware_ready() ignores.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c | 7 -------
 1 file changed, 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
index 3e742dbed..3b457474f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -83,13 +83,6 @@ static int ath12k_core_rfkill_config(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 	if (ath12k_acpi_get_disable_rfkill(ab))
 		return 0;
 
-	/* Peach borrows the WCN7850 parameters, whose rfkill GPIO 48
-	 * is not wired on this module: the firmware then reports the
-	 * radio hard-blocked. Stock has no Wi-Fi rfkill switch.
-	 */
-	if (ab->id.device == 0x110e)
-		return 0;
-
 	for (i = 0; i < ab->num_radios; i++) {
 		ar = ab->pdevs[i].ar;
 
